Measured on 2026-09-29 at develop 3627cb2. 31 TS/JS files use Deno.* APIs: 733 call sites. Breakdown: Deno.test 158; file-system calls (writeTextFile 127, mkdir 47, readTextFile 38, remove 35, readFile 24, makeTempDir 22, stat 21, symlink 17, rename 13, readDirSync 13, copyFile 13, chmod 13, realPath 11, lstat 8, cwd 6, writeFile 5, open 3, readLink 2, chdir 2); Deno.Command 47 constructions in 21 files (39 .output() calls, 2 .spawn() calls) plus 5 Deno.CommandOutput types; Deno.execPath 19 (all spawn the deno executable with Deno subcommands such as run, test, check); env 20; exit 14; errors.NotFound 12 and AlreadyExists 3; args 18; kill 1; exitCode 1; permissions.query 1.
@deno/shim-deno 0.19.2 (npm, MIT, denoland/node_shims, last publish 2026-03-24) provides every used API except Deno.Command and Deno.exitCode; its Deno.test only pushes test definitions to an array and needs a separate runner. Upstream PR denoland/node_shims#183 'feat: add shim for Command' has been open since 2024-02-28, is marked blocked, returns success:false for exit code 0, defaults output() to inherited stdio, and throws 'Not implemented' from spawn().
Probe: with a two-line preload that sets globalThis.Deno to the shim, scripts/validate_plugins.ts ran unchanged on Node 24.19 and printed the same PASS report as on Deno. Test files failed at their first new Deno.Command.
@std/testing/snapshot (used by scripts/cli_contract_test.ts) reads the Deno test context's origin and name and calls Deno.writeTextFileSync, Deno.permissions.query, Deno.inspect and Deno.args; node:test in Node 24.19 provides TestContext.name, TestContext.filePath and its own t.assert.snapshot with a different snapshot file format. @std/testing/mock stub is plain JavaScript.
Node 24.19 built-ins cover every used API: node:fs/promises, node:child_process (spawn, execFile), node:test, process.env, process.argv, process.exit, process.exitCode.
